The final step in the planning section is that you adopt this the affordable housing plan into your plan of development as an addendum to your plan of conservation and development,

00:39:33.860 --> 00:39:40.665
which is important because it's official town policy then. It's not just a plan that you had to do. It becomes official town policy

00:39:40.745 --> 00:39:43.065
in your plan of conservation and development.

00:39:43.225 --> 00:39:49.385
So when you look to the plan of conservation and development you see that and you justify the recommendations that you're making

00:39:49.705 --> 00:39:50.585
to change things.

00:39:51.960 --> 00:39:53.160
The first one

00:39:54.200 --> 00:40:01.960
gets a little into the weeds about it's a little complicated. Public Act 20 one-twenty nine said towns must provide accessory apartments

00:40:02.040 --> 00:40:05.625
and we talked about this and Jed and I talked about this and and

00:40:05.705 --> 00:40:10.585
the problem is just like right where I am right now at Lake Besik

00:40:10.745 --> 00:40:12.265
in Middlefield,

00:40:12.585 --> 00:40:17.225
providing accessory apartments here where there's a high density of housing already

00:40:18.200 --> 00:40:20.520
creates creates potential groundwater

00:40:20.520 --> 00:40:25.720
issues and lake issues and all kinds of different issues where it's already very dense.

00:40:26.280 --> 00:40:27.320
So again,

00:40:27.640 --> 00:40:30.440
I would first recommend that the Commission

00:40:30.525 --> 00:40:39.165
and the Planning and the Board of Selectmen opt out of Public Act 20 one-twenty nine so you are not forced to provide

00:40:39.645 --> 00:40:40.765
and allow

00:40:40.845 --> 00:40:45.540
accessory apartments in the Andover Lake District because you wouldn't want to allow

00:40:45.620 --> 00:40:47.540
conceivably by right

00:40:48.260 --> 00:40:51.860
every other house along Andover Lake becoming

00:40:51.860 --> 00:40:55.300
a house and accessory apartment if the

00:40:57.235 --> 00:40:59.075
septic system could support it.

00:40:59.475 --> 00:41:05.075
So I recommend that you opt out and that's pretty detailed but I'm just that's one of the recommendations.

00:41:05.235 --> 00:41:10.195
But then after opting out in the Andover Rural Design District, I definitely think you should comply with

00:41:10.595 --> 00:41:18.410
the recommendations of the Public Act and increase from 800 to a thousand square feet remove the special permit requirements for detached units

00:41:18.570 --> 00:41:19.210
to

00:41:19.690 --> 00:41:25.130
give the message to the state that yes Andover is understands and is making the right strides.

00:41:25.975 --> 00:41:26.535
This

00:41:27.015 --> 00:41:30.855
next one is what you're talking we're talking about Leanne is the

00:41:31.255 --> 00:41:35.255
duplexes amend the ARD zone to allow as of right

00:41:35.735 --> 00:41:38.295
two to four two three or four unit structures

00:41:38.690 --> 00:41:43.330
on larger lots including design guidelines to protect the rural single

00:41:43.330 --> 00:41:45.010
family residential character.

00:41:45.650 --> 00:41:46.130
So

00:41:46.530 --> 00:41:53.330
small towns get a real bad rap because they have 90% of their town is zoned single family residential

00:41:53.515 --> 00:41:56.635
and that's all they allow on a two acre lot.

00:41:57.995 --> 00:42:00.555
For Andover, I believe it's our 60,000

00:42:00.715 --> 00:42:06.475
square foot lot. So that's all you allow is a single family home. A 60,000 square foot lot

00:42:06.795 --> 00:42:09.195
even with Well and Septic could support

00:42:09.530 --> 00:42:12.730
a duplex or a three family or four family.

00:42:13.530 --> 00:42:17.130
Those are things that you might want to consider. For instance on

00:42:17.290 --> 00:42:18.090
a

00:42:18.330 --> 00:42:21.690
two or three plus acre lot you can allow

00:42:21.905 --> 00:42:31.505
a two family or three family because the whole idea is it becomes much more economical and more affordable if you have more units on one lot.

00:42:31.745 --> 00:42:36.740
So that's a recommendation that you should really look into and think about doing.

00:42:37.140 --> 00:42:43.220
But of course keeping design guidelines so it looks like just a big old farmhouse or something not a typical

00:42:44.900 --> 00:42:47.220
urban two family or three family.

00:42:51.395 --> 00:42:53.315
Traditionally in towns

00:42:53.315 --> 00:42:56.675
mobile homes were always considered the low

00:42:57.155 --> 00:42:59.155
income housing for rural communities.

00:43:01.070 --> 00:43:03.710
Small towns have prohibited

00:43:03.870 --> 00:43:07.550
mobile homes. Andover is no different. You prohibit them but

00:43:08.030 --> 00:43:10.110
the latest public act 20

00:43:10.190 --> 00:43:14.830
one-twenty nine has said that you have to treat mobile home and manufactured homes

00:43:15.475 --> 00:43:19.555
meeting the safe definition they have to be 24 feet wide or something like that.

00:43:20.035 --> 00:43:24.915
You have to treat them just like a single family home so no more can you prohibit

00:43:24.995 --> 00:43:37.670
mobile homes. So if somebody wants to put a mobile home on a lot because it's the most affordable way to do it You have to allow it just like you allow any other single family home so you need to eliminate that prohibited use section.

00:43:40.310 --> 00:43:45.645
We have one section that I believe we put in when I was there section 14.14

00:43:45.645 --> 00:43:47.485
prd for older persons

